# The binary digits of a number, most significant first.

π' → A
? → n
1 → p

π' → B              # Find the largest power of two p that is <= n.
(1 ∸ (p·2 ∸ n))·C + (1 ∩ (p·2 ∸ n))·D → π

π' → C
p·2 → p
B → π

π' → D              # Print the digit at p, remove it, halve p. Stop when p is 0.
n:p → ?
n mod p → n
p:2 → p
(1 ∩ p)·D → π
